What will you do?

Do you have an affinity for technology or experience in technical production, and are you handy with practical work? Are you also looking for a long-term job opportunity? Then look no further!

As a Field Service Technician, you will visit various organizations, ranging from large government institutions and universities to hospitals. The work requires specialized skills, for which you will receive internal training.

Your responsibilities include:

- Maintenance and renovation of air handling systems;
- Cleaning and gas-free preparation of installations within the chemical industry;
- Collaborating with various clients to ensure technical installations function optimally.

Who are you?

In addition to an interest in technology and technical insight, you have:

- A VCA certificate or willingness to obtain one;
- A valid Category B driving license;
- Strong communication skills, customer friendliness, and initiative;
- Good command of the English and/or Dutch language.

Are you a natural leader with experience in logistics? Do you enjoy managing people while continuously improving operational processes? Then this could be the perfect opportunity for you!

We are looking for a Warehouse Supervisor to join an international logistics organization. In this role, you will be responsible for the daily warehouse operation, ensuring your team works safely, efficiently, and delivers the highest quality standards.

What will you do?
As a Warehouse Supervisor, you will lead a team of approximately 15 to 30 warehouse employees and temporary staff. You will be actively present on the warehouse floor and ensure that daily operations run smoothly.

Your responsibilities include:

- Coordinating inbound, storage, and outbound logistics activities;
- Leading, coaching, and motivating warehouse employees;
- Monitoring productivity, planning, and operational quality;
- Ensuring accurate administrative processing within the Warehouse Management System (WMS);
- Identifying operational bottlenecks and driving process improvements;
- Ensuring compliance with safety, quality, and company procedures;
- Conducting performance reviews, coaching sessions, and absence management;
- Working closely with Customer Service and the Warehouse Manager to continuously improve customer satisfaction.

You are a hands-on and motivated supervisor who knows how to inspire a team while maintaining focus on operational excellence.

You also have:

- An MBO Level 4 qualification, preferably in Logistics or Supply Chain;
- At least 2 years of leadership experience within a logistics or production environment;
- Good command of Dutch and/or English;
- Strong communication and leadership skills;
- Experience with warehouse operations and WMS systems;
- You can provide a valid Certificate of Conduct (VOG). If your VOG is approved, Olympia will reimburse the cost of €41.35. If your VOG is not approved, the cost will be at your own expense.
